From 3975513f664213c4947bdcbebbd25deb98214202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:20:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/53] dhcpd: lease on every interface, one default route

dhcpd watches netcfg ifaces/ and gets a lease on each interface,
including ones that appear later, with a 5 s wait per reply and retries.
Replies are taken only with our transaction ID and MAC. The default
route and name server come from the first wired interface with a lease,
else from Wi-Fi. dhcpd -i <iface> keeps the old one-shot behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
